 4. Quick hits 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 Cowboy Space debuted its new "Big Iron" rocket design on Oct. 26. Photo: Courtesy of Cowboy Space

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 🚀 California's Vandenberg Space Force Base broke its all-time launch record .

 The big picture: The SpaceX Falcon 9 rocket launch on Tuesday marked the 72nd launch that the Space Force supported from the base, according to the service . 💭 My thought bubble: There are still two months left in this year, meaning the West Coast's launch range is heading for never-before-seen heights. 👀 Tim Morrison, a former Boeing defense executive and National Security Council official , has joined Washington Harbour Partners.

 Follow the money: Washington Harbour, based in Virginia, has backed many well-known defense-tech players, including Apex Space , SpaceX and Turion Space. 💭 Colin's thought bubble: Morrison's warning and rationale are worth a read. Check that out, here . ⛰️ Appalachia and the Midwest want in on the space game, my colleague Ryan Deto reported yesterday. 

 By the numbers: The tri-state region has more than 1,000 space industry firms that have brought in more than $9.5 billion in federal deals over the last four years, according to the Keystone Space Collaborative. 💭 My thought bubble: California, Florida and Texas are the big space hubs, but new initiatives, like Trump's Space Academy, could pull investment away from the coasts. 🇵🇱 Poland will host a new Patriot missile maintenance facility, the Pentagon announced on Tuesday.

 What they're saying: Michael P. Duffey, under secretary of defense for acquisition and sustainment said NATO is "serious about deterrence, and ready to back our words with action." 💭 Colin's thought bubble: The new facility is about as close to Russia as you can comfortably get. 
 
