 5. Check this out 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 
 An Air Force Research Laboratory cargo pod for training and exercising recovery operations. Photo: Courtesy of SpaceX/via DVIDS

 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Rocket Door Dash? The Air Force Research Laboratory said it delivered military cargo using a SpaceX Starfall capsule last week. 

 Since 2021 , the military has been exploring if cargo aboard a launched rocket can be delivered to a location back on Earth in less than an hour. The pod inside was filled with survival equipment, water and two MREs (meals ready to eat). Why it matters: Space-based cargo delivery could make dangerous battlefield deliveries safer in the future.

 AFRL is working with multiple firms including Blue Origin, Rocket Lab, Sierra Space, Anduril, Inversion Space and Outpost Space, according to the press release . Fun fact: Years ago, I wrote about the South Carolina factory where they make MREs.

 In my opinion, the Italian sausage with peppers MRE isn't half bad! 
 
